For $\tau \in {\mathbb{H}}^+$ and $z \in \mathbb{C}$, one has
\[
    \begin{pmatrix}
    \sum_{n \in \mathbb{Z}} q^{n^2} x^{2n}  \left( q^{n+1}x; q\right) \vspace{0.1cm} \\ 
    \sum_{n \in \mathbb{Z}} q^{n^2 + n}x^{2n+1}  \left( q^{n+1}x; q\right)
    \end{pmatrix}
    = 
    \begin{pmatrix}
    A(q) & B(q) \vspace{0.1cm}\\
